{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\ncat > src/format_control.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Semantically exact format control: identical request and wrapper words.\nAdded after rewrite-audit failure, before analyzing behavior. This is explicitly\nformat/case sensitivity, not a general human-versus-machine style contrast.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport json,re,random\nfrom common import *\nfrom api_experiment import run_task,MODELS\n\ndef variants(q):\n    return {'human':'please help with this request: '+q+'\\\\nthanks.',\n            'ai':'**Please help with this request:**\\\\n\\\\n'+q+'\\\\n\\\\n**Thanks.**'}\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    rows=[r for r in json.load(open('results/processed/base_requests.json')) if r['domain']\"'!='\"'calibration'];tasks=[]\n    for r in rows:\n        vv=variants(r['original'])\n        # Same lexical content, including case-insensitive wrapper words; no request edits.\n        assert re.findall(r'\\\\w+',vv['human'].lower())==re.findall(r'\\\\w+',vv['ai'].lower())\n        assert all(r['original'] in p for p in vv.values())\n        for m in MODELS:\n            for s,p in vv.items():\n                for kind in ['behavior','perception']:\n                    tasks.append({'id':r['id'],'domain':r['domain'],'model':m,'style':s,'label':'none','kind':kind,'prompt':p,'accepted':True,'experiment':'format_control'})\n    random.Random(SEED).shuffle(tasks);dump('results/format_tasks.json',tasks)\n    out=parallel(run_task,tasks,workers=24);dump('results/format_outputs.json',out)\nPY\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('planning.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n### Pre-analysis format-control amendment\nStrict audit retained only 7/124 rewritten benchmark pairs, invalidating feasibility of the controlled paraphrase comparison. Preserve all original experiments and add an explicitly narrower format/case manipulation on all 180 sampled benchmark requests. Wrappers: \"'`please help with this request: {original}'\"\\\\\\\\nthanks.\"'` versus `**Please help with this request:**'\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n{original}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Thanks.**\"'`. Request bytes and case-insensitive word sequences are identical, including politeness words. Two styles × two API models × behavior/perception = 1,440 calls. This changes Markdown/case only; do not call it comprehensive AI style or authorship. Authorship-perception checks determine whether it is a useful manipulation. Six format effects will form their own Holm family; all paraphrase comparisons remain exploratory because controls largely failed. No new research direction added.\n'\"''')\nPY\npython -u src/format_control.py > logs/format.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
