{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/judge.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"    if t.get('kind')=='perception':return t\\\", \\\"    if t.get('kind')=='perception':return t\\\\n    if t.get('error') or not t.get('text','').strip():return {**t,'score_error':'No assistant response; provider block/error/empty output', 'score':{}}\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('planning.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n\n### Truncation correction after first-pass diagnostics\nThe 256-token API budget frequently truncated opinions before a clear choice and longer benign tasks. Re-run every available API behavioral cell at 1,536 output tokens (same prompt/model/decoding), retaining the initial run as a sensitivity dataset. Provider-blocked cells remain missing and are not recoded as refusal or task failure. Report initial and expanded invalid/truncation rates. This is outcome-independent budget expansion across all arms after an instrumentation problem, not selective retry of unfavorable outcomes. Local 128-token generations are explicitly a short-response refusal/alignment readout; capability checks and logit diagnostics will accompany them.\n''')\nPY\ncat > src/extend_api.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Uniform larger response budget to repair first-pass truncation, keeping originals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport json,random\nfrom common import *\n\ndef extend(t):\n    if t['kind']=='perception' or t.get('error'):return t\n    r=call(t['model'],t['prompt'],max_tokens=1536,tag='behavior_extended')\n    return {**t,'initial_key':t['key'],'key':r['key'],'text':content(r),'error':r.get('error'),'finish_reason':r.get('response',{}).get('choices',[{}])[0].get('finish_reason'),'max_tokens':1536}\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    rows=[]\n    for name in ['api','format']:\n        rows.extend([{**r,'dataset':name} for r in json.load(open(f'results/{name}_outputs.json'))])\n    random.Random(SEED).shuffle(rows);out=parallel(extend,rows,workers=24)\n    for name in ['api','format']:dump(f'results/{name}_outputs_long.json',[r for r in out if r['dataset']==name])\nPY\npython -u src/extend_api.py > logs/extend_api.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
